{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And they conceived.</b> Rashi explained: even though a woman does not conceive from the first act of relations, these controlled themselves and expelled their maidenhood. The reading is עדותן in Bereshit Rabbah, meaning their virginity, and the proof is from Bereshit Rabbah: ״ואלה בתולי בתי״ — עדות בתי. And we do not adopt the reading ראשונה as the world says."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The note distinguishes between the reading עדותן ('their testimony/proof,' read midrashically as 'their virginity') in Bereshit Rabbah and the common reading ראשונה ('first'); ראיה refers to a textual proof for the reading עדותן from the midrashic interpretation of ואלה בתולי בתי."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:40.783102397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}